Syntax: kwave <victim>

Kinetic wave projects a focused burst of telekinetic force at an enemy,
attempting to physically knock them from their feet. Unlike the mental
attacks of psionic blast or psychic crush, this power manifests as raw
physical force generated through the power of the mind.

A fully successful attack knocks the victim to the ground, sending them
sprawling. Mounted opponents may be knocked from their steeds. The force
of the impact deals damage and leaves the victim momentarily stunned,
creating an opening for follow-up attacks.

Even when the wave fails to completely knock an opponent down, it still
strikes with considerable force, dealing damage through the partial
impact. The difference between a complete success and partial success
depends on both skill and the target's ability to resist.

Victims knocked down by the wave may have their concentration disrupted
if they were attempting to cast spells or perform other focused actions.

The power initiates combat if the psionicist is not already engaged with
the target. If used in combat, it can be directed at the current opponent
without specifying a target.

Kinetic wave is an advanced power requiring significant mastery of
psionics to learn. It cannot be used while focusing your mind.

See Also: PSIONICS, TELEKINESIS, MIND FOCUS

